# 🛡️ Home Network Asset Inventory

Setting up an asset management inventory for a home-based small business to identify network devices and protect sensitive data.

---

## 📊 Device Inventory

| Device ID | Device Name | Owner | Location | Connection | Sensitive Data / Scope | Sensitivity Level |
| :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |
| **AST-001** | Workstation Laptop | Business Owner | Home Office | Ethernet / Wi-Fi | Client records, financial files, admin access | **HIGH** |
| **AST-002** | Personal Smartphone | Business Owner | Mobile / House | Wi-Fi | Business email, 2FA authenticator apps | **MEDIUM** |
| **AST-003** | Smart TV | Shared / Household | Living Room | Wi-Fi | Streaming media (No business data) | **LOW** |

---

## 🏷️ Sensitivity Levels

- 🔴 **HIGH:** Contains critical business data or admin access. High impact if compromised.
- 🟡 **MEDIUM:** Holds secondary access like email or 2FA. Moderate risk.
- 🟢 **LOW:** Household IoT device with no sensitive files. Low direct risk.

---

## 🔐 Recommended Security Steps

1. **Network Isolation:** Put Smart TVs and IoT devices on a separate Guest/IoT Wi-Fi network.
2. **Access Control:** Turn on full disk encryption (BitLocker) and 2FA on the business laptop and phone.
3. **Updates:** Keep all device operating systems updated automatically.
